Licensing of the FTSRG TDK template
=================================

Original reusable contributions: Copyright (c) 2026 Martin Farkas.
Retain other authors' existing copyright and attribution notices.

This repository contains material under several terms. A file's existing
license or provenance notice takes precedence over the defaults below.

Original reusable code and tooling
---------------------------------

Original scripts, build configuration, tests, project scaffolding and template
implementation are licensed under the MIT License in LICENSES/MIT.txt. This
includes original code under scripts/, infra/, paper/scripts/, presentation/
scripts/, and original code/proof/benchmark examples. Original TeX implementation
and reusable theme modifications are included; inherited implementations retain
their stated terms.

Original guide and slide prose
------------------------------

Original guide text, explanatory worked examples, onboarding instructions and
slide prose are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(CC BY 4.0):

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The complete terms are in LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt. Attribute the reused original
material to Martin Farkas, FTSRG TDK template, and preserve any additional named
creators and existing attributions. Include the source and license links and
indicate modifications. Original executable examples use the MIT terms above.

Source: https://github.com/FTSRG-BCLab-TDK/TDK-template

Inherited material and exceptions
--------------------------------

- presentation/PROVENANCE.md identifies the presentation sources, preserved AVM
  MIT notice, OFL font licenses and institutional artwork permission. Keep those
  notices with exported assets. BME/FTSRG logos and graph backgrounds are retained
  under Martin's confirmed redistribution permission; this file does not relabel
  them MIT or CC BY or grant new rights to the institutional marks.
- paper/tdkieee.bst and other inherited bibliography/LaTeX implementations retain
  their own license and attribution notices. This file does not replace LPPL,
  GPL, or other terms embedded in inherited files or their history.
- Faculty documents, quoted research, reproduced paper figures and other
  third-party material retain their source terms. Cite and preserve the recorded
  provenance; inclusion here does not assign a new license to them.
- Installed tools and dependencies retain their own licenses.

Student projects and selected publications
-----------------------------------------

These grants cover the reusable template contributions described above. Creating
a project from the template does not automatically license new student papers,
research code, proofs, datasets, notes or slides. Their authors select the terms
for their own contributions and preserve the inherited template notices.

A publication package must identify the license for each selected part and carry
its required notices. Do not label an entire mixed archive MIT or CC BY merely
because it contains template material. Private scratch and unpublished research
are not implicitly selected for publication.
